From 7976cabc1cbc61220ec10a6344bab44558551271 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:00:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v5 05/10] wifi: rtw89: use AP self role for monitor interfaces

rtw89_vif_type_mapping() leaves net_type and self_role zero for
NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR, i.e. RTW89_NET_TYPE_NO_LINK and
RTW89_SELF_ROLE_CLIENT. rtw89_mac_vif_init() then sends the join info
H2C for the monitor MAC ID with this client role.

On RTL8852AE (firmware 0.13.36.2), frames queued on the monitor
MAC ID are never transmitted in this configuration: raw frames
injected on a standalone monitor interface are accepted by the driver
but do not show up on the air. With self_role set to
RTW89_SELF_ROLE_AP the same frames are transmitted, and aireplay-ng
injection tests succeed.

The firmware behaviour was determined by testing only. self_role is
consumed solely by the join info and role maintain H2C commands, and
net_type stays RTW89_NET_TYPE_NO_LINK, so port configuration is not
affected. Set both fields explicitly for monitor interfaces.

Signed-off-by: Enver Ikromov <owner@ph4ntom-rev.uz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
index 0744c31..e82285a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/core.c
@@ -5744,6 +5744,8 @@ void rtw89_vif_type_mapping(struct rtw89_vif_link *rtwvif_link, bool assoc)
 		rtwvif_link->self_role = RTW89_SELF_ROLE_CLIENT;
 		break;
 	case NL80211_IFTYPE_MONITOR:
+		rtwvif_link->net_type = RTW89_NET_TYPE_NO_LINK;
+		rtwvif_link->self_role = RTW89_SELF_ROLE_AP;
 		break;
 	default:
 		WARN_ON(1);
